        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Falcon 1690-EO, Falcon 36\" Vertical Rod Exit Device</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Falcon 1690 panic device blends the utility of a vertical rod application with the appearance of a traditional panic device. It is non-handed and reversible with a contoured cross bar that will fit doors up to 36 inches wide. The Falcon Concealed Vertical Rod Crossbar Exit Device requires a 1-3/4 inch minimum mounting surface.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features and Specifications</b> of the Falcon Concealed Vertical Panic Device:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Doors Thickness: 1-3⁄4\" thick metal doors.</li>\r\n<li>Door Width: Up to 36\"</li>\r\n<li>Bar Projection: 3-3⁄8\" in neutral position, 2-3⁄8\" in dogged position.</li>\r\n<li>Pushbar Height: 2-1⁄2\".</li>\r\n<li>Stile Width: 1-3⁄4\" minimum.</li>\r\n<li>Door Height: Up to 84\" (7 Ft)</li>\r\n<li>Dogging: Hex key dogging standard</li>\r\n<li>Certified ANSI A156.3 grade 1 standards.</li>\r\n<li>Handing: Reversible, non-handed</li>\r\n<li>Fasteners: All machine screw mounting. Device mounting fasteners are concealed, latch fasteners are exposed to egress side.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<i>Sold Individually</i>\r\n</p>",
